From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kebab refactor <kebab@local.invalid>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 14:04:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: fix NULL dereference reading the DP test debugfs
 files

Reading any of /sys/kernel/debug/dri/0/DP-1/dp_test_active,
dp_test_data or dp_test_type oopses the kernel on external
DisplayPort:

  Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 00000000000000a8
  Internal error: Oops: 0000000096000004 [#1] SMP
  pc : msm_dp_test_active_show+0x14/0x60

0xa8 is the offset of drm_connector::status, so debug->connector is
NULL. msm_dp_display_debugfs_init() passes
dp->msm_dp_display.connector to msm_dp_debug_init(), and for external
DP that is still NULL at the time debugfs is created -- the connector
is created later by the bridge. msm_dp_debug_init() validates dev,
panel and link but not connector, stores the NULL, and all four
handlers dereference it unconditionally.

A debugfs read should not be able to oops the kernel. Check the
pointer in the three show handlers and in msm_dp_test_active_write(),
treating a connector that does not exist yet the same way as one that
is disconnected.

Reproduced on sm8250 (OnePlus 8T) by cat'ing the three files as root
while a DisplayPort sink was attached; three consecutive oopses, one
per file, each killing only the reader.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_debug.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_debug.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_debug.c
index cf3838fcd..63f960be5 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_debug.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_debug.c
@@ -92,7 +92,7 @@ static int msm_dp_test_data_show(struct seq_file *m, void *data)
 	const struct drm_connector *connector = debug->connector;
 	u32 bpc;
 
-	if (connector->status == connector_status_connected) {
+	if (connector && connector->status == connector_status_connected) {
 		bpc = debug->link->test_video.test_bit_depth;
 		seq_printf(m, "hdisplay: %d\n",
 				debug->link->test_video.test_h_width);
@@ -113,7 +113,7 @@ static int msm_dp_test_type_show(struct seq_file *m, void *data)
 	const struct msm_dp_debug_private *debug = m->private;
 	const struct drm_connector *connector = debug->connector;
 
-	if (connector->status == connector_status_connected)
+	if (connector && connector->status == connector_status_connected)
 		seq_printf(m, "%02x", DP_TEST_LINK_VIDEO_PATTERN);
 	else
 		seq_puts(m, "0");
@@ -144,7 +144,7 @@ static ssize_t msm_dp_test_active_write(struct file *file,
 
 	DRM_DEBUG_DRIVER("Copied %d bytes from user\n", (unsigned int)len);
 
-	if (connector->status == connector_status_connected) {
+	if (connector && connector->status == connector_status_connected) {
 		status = kstrtoint(input_buffer, 10, &val);
 		if (status < 0) {
 			kfree(input_buffer);
@@ -170,7 +170,7 @@ static int msm_dp_test_active_show(struct seq_file *m, void *data)
 	struct msm_dp_debug_private *debug = m->private;
 	struct drm_connector *connector = debug->connector;
 
-	if (connector->status == connector_status_connected) {
+	if (connector && connector->status == connector_status_connected) {
 		if (debug->panel->video_test)
 			seq_puts(m, "1");
 		else
